-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1107: a WITHIN that reads a name the rule defines with
-- WHERE, or a value an event carried, is not worked out, and the reason says
-- which it reads. (given.l4 has the rule's own input.)

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Alice, Bob
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Pay HAS amount IS A NUMBER
    ship

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`where local` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST ship WITHIN period LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"
  WHERE period MEANS 20

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`event carried` MEANS
    PARTY Alice MUST Pay n WITHIN 10
    HENCE (PARTY Bob MUST ship WITHIN n LEST BREACH BY Bob BECAUSE "late")

#TRACE `event carried` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES Pay 4 AT 1
